      "name": "branch-archaeology",
      "title": "Branch archaeology: what each branch holds that main does not",
      "description": "Classify every remote branch against the default branch (merged, landed by squash or cherry-pick, partially landed, unlanded, undetermined) by commit ancestry, patch-id and merge-tree, not by subject line. Report only, never delete. A branch touching content or mathematics is a salvage-review item and never a delete candidate. Covers the treeless fetch that makes thousands of branches cheap, caching by tip sha, and the report's shape. Read before answering \"which branches can go?\" or \"what work never landed?\".",
